🎮 PIXEL DASH

🇬🇧 EN

A 2D pixel-art platformer inspired by Celeste. You play as a little mountaineer climbing a mountain to reach the summit his grandfather used to tell him about.

How to Play

Open index.html in your browser. No installation required. The game works offline.

Features

Room-based campaign: Over 70 rooms across 13 chapters. Each room introduces a new mechanic or combination of mechanics.
Responsive movement: Running, variable-height jumping, double jump, wall jump, eight-direction dash, wall grabbing and climbing.
Level elements: Spikes, springs (up, down and sideways), air currents, ice, moving platforms, crumbling and falling platforms, blinking blocks and lasers.
Gem doors: Some exits remain locked until you collect enough gems.
Mini-movie: Tom's story told through 20 scenes.
Characters: Six mountaineers, each with their own trail (hair, ribbon, flame, snow, pixels and rainbow).
Level editor: Create your own levels and chapters, then share them using short codes (PD2: for a level, PC2: for a chapter).
Library: Locally save your levels and chapters, and import shared codes.
Local multiplayer: Play with a friend over the same Wi-Fi using WebRTC and copy-paste codes. No server required.
Languages: English (default) and French, switchable using flags.
Update log: Displays changes with each new version.

Controls

Action	Keyboard
Move	Arrow keys or WASD
Jump	Space, Z, C or K
Dash	X, Shift or L
Pause	Escape or P
Restart room	R
Sound	M

Structure

pixel-dash-v7.html: The complete game in a single file.
pixel-dash-web/: Hosting-ready version with a manifest and service worker (installable on Chromebook).

Technical

Built entirely with JavaScript, HTML and Canvas, without external libraries. Physics runs at a fixed 1/60-second timestep. Rooms are described using ASCII text, making them easy to share.

